  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Area of the cross-section of a wire is measured using a screw gauge. The pitch of the main scale is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. The circular scale has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> divisions and for one full rotation of the circular scale, the main scale shifts by two divisions. The measured readings are listed below.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 350px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><strong>Measurement condition</strong></td>\t\t\t<td><strong>Main scale reading</strong></td>\t\t\t<td><strong>Circular scale reading</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Two arms of gauge touching each other without wire</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;division</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;divisions</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Attempt-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>: With wire</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;divisions</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> divisions</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Attempt-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>: With wire</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;divisions</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math> divisions</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>What are the diameter and cross-sectional area of the wire measured using the screw gauge?</p>",
    "image": null
  },
